#!groovy
//noinspection GroovyUnusedAssignment
@Library("Infrastructure@2.13.1") _

def type = "nodejs"
def product = "deed-poll"
def component = "admin"

// `product` / `component` are the pair the shared Terraform root was written against: this app reads the
// `deed-poll-${env}` vault, and its secrets are prefixed `admin-` per component. The Jenkinsfile this repo
// carried before the re-scaffold declared `rpe` / `expressjs-template` — template boilerplate that had
// never been configured. See `.business_context/DEED_POLL_INFRA_PLAN.md`.
//
// The library is pinned to the same version as `hmcts/deed-poll-infra`'s `withInfraPipeline`, so the
// product's two pipelines move together. Pinning is the estate norm — pcs and pt both pin. Reconfirmed
// against that repo's own `Jenkinsfile_CNP` on 2026-09-10: both are `Infrastructure@2.4.4`. Bump both or
// neither.
//
// Empty body deliberately:
//   - secrets reach this app through the Helm chart's `keyVaults:` block (a properties volume), not
//     `loadVaultSecrets`, so there is nothing for the pipeline to inject into the build;
//   - `yarn build` is not called here because the Dockerfile runs it, so a type error fails the image
//     build rather than passing unnoticed (`yarn test` transpiles without type-checking);
//   - there is no `Jenkinsfile_nightly` — see `docs/PIPELINES.md` for that and for the onboarding work
//     this pipeline still needs before it can deploy;
//   - **no `enableE2eTest()`, and that is a decision rather than an omission.** `AppPipelineConfig.e2eTest`
//     defaults false, so `yarn test:e2e` runs in no pipeline at all. It cannot: the journeys need a
//     caseworker signed in through `rse-idam-simulator` and fixtures from the in-memory api mock on :3200,
//     and a deployed environment has neither. The post-deploy gate is `yarn test:smoke` instead. Note that
//     `sectionDeployToAKS` also runs the e2e suite for any PR carrying the GitHub label `enable_e2e_test` —
//     so it is one label away from running against a deployment it cannot pass. Don't add that label.
withPipeline(type, product, component) {
}
